# MediaPipe Pose Quick Notes

## Core idea

```python
results = pose.process(image)
```

- `results.pose_landmarks` = body landmarks for the current frame.
- `None` means no person was detected.
- If detected, you get 33 landmarks.

## Landmark values

Each landmark has:
- `x`: left-right (normalized 0..1)
- `y`: up-down (normalized 0..1)
- `z`: relative depth (not true meters)
- `visibility`: confidence for that point



mp_pose.POSE_CONNECTIONS
whick landmark is connected to which



# to see all available landmark names
for lndmrk in mp_pose.PoseLandmark:
    print(lndmrk)

# to access detected landmarks from current frame
if results.pose_landmarks:
    landmarks = results.pose_landmarks.landmark
    left_shoulder = landmarks[mp_pose.PoseLandmark.LEFT_SHOULDER.value]
    print(left_shoulder.x, left_shoulder.y, left_shoulder.z, left_shoulder.visibility)